WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.460
There are two ways to solve for the square root of a number.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.580
We can either use a calculator.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.900
Of course! Everybody would love to use this option.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.440
And the other way is to solve it manually.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.840
Manually too we can solve it in two different ways.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.200
One, by using the prime factorisation method which we have already seen.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.560
We split the number to its prime factors.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.380
And then choose one number from each pair.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.100
The other method which we will look at in this video,

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.300
is called the long division method .

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.540
The name sounds fancy, but don't worry,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:41.140
if you follow the steps given in this video, you will never go wrong.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.980
But why can't we just use prime factorisation every time?

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.620
Well, if the number is large, it will take us a lot of time

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.040
to reduce it to its prime factors and

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.980
the chances of going wrong are very high.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.740
Hence, prime factorization is useful only for small numbers.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.920
And for large numbers we can use the long division method.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.160
Let's solve a couple of examples

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.900
to understand how the long division method works.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.540
Look at the number 8,281.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.780
If we have to reduce this number to its prime factors,

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:16.880
we would first have to think of

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.860
all the divisibility rules and so on and that would take us a lot of time.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.380
So for such large numbers, we use the long division method.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.740
The first thing we need to do in the long division method is to draw lines like this.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:35.620
A line on top and a line to the left of the number.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.480
When you draw a line on top of the number,

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.760
remember to leave some space above the number.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.140
Once you're done drawing these lines you're ready for the first step.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:50.700
The first step is to mark pairs of digits from the unit's end.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.680
The unit's end is the number one!

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.720
So we mark pairs of digits from right-hand side.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.780
This becomes our first pair from the right! The number 81.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:07.680
We continue to mark pairs till we cover all digits of the number.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.140
The next pair will be 82.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.580
So the first step was simple!

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:18.400
We just mark pairs from the right which gives us 2 pairs 82 and 81.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.980
Now we look at the first pair from the left which is 82.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.260
In the second step we have to find the perfect

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:30.120
square which is equal to or lower than 82.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.140
Since 82 is not a perfect square,

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:36.800
we choose the perfect square lower than 82.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.800
The perfect square just lower than 82 is 81.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.340
Even 64 is a perfect square lower than 82.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:45.920
But remember,

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.520
we always choose the one which is closest.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.880
We know that 9 squared equals 81.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.060
We just found out the most crucial number. It's the number 9.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.840
9 is basically the square root of the closest perfect square.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:04.680
We write the number 9 here to the left of the number.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.120
This was actually the most important step of the long division process,

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.740
to find the first number!

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.880
The next step is one of the easiest steps.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.440
But it's a step where most the students get confused.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:22.560
The step says, multiply above and add below .

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:28.580
But what do we multiply and what do we add? It is the same number 9.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.860
Let's focus on multiplying above first.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:36.160
We multiply 9 with 9 and write the product here.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.800
So the 9 you're multiplying is written on top.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:46.220
Now let's come to add below! We add 9 with 9 and write the sum underneath

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.200
9 plus 9 gives us 18.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:54.480
We multiply the same number with itself above and wrote the product here.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.240
And we added the same number with itself and wrote the sum here.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.160
Remember! When we multiply or add we're doing

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.160
the operation with the same digit.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.340
In this case, it's 9.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:12.520
So we have completed three steps: first, we found the pairs from the right,

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:17.520
second, we found the perfect square and wrote a square root here,

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:21.540
third we multiplied above and add it below.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.660
If you observed it well,

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.420
you could see that, I have left some space next to the sum of nines.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.260
That space is kept for the box.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:32.600
So we draw an empty box here.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.840
And inside this box, we will be writing some digit.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.640
Our next aim is to find this digit.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.860
The next three steps are super simple.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:45.240
We just subtract the product from the number above it.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.840
The product we got was 81, the number above it is 82.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:55.500
We subtract 81 from 82 and get 1.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.960
And then we get the next pair down. The next pair is 81.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.220
So we write it next to 1.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.340
Then we draw the same box above and below.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:12.660
Above we draw it next to 9 and below we draw it under the original box.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:16.420
The digits contained in each of these boxes are the same.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.360
The next step according to me is the

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.860
most interesting step of the long division method.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:26.340
We use trial and error to find the digit in the boxes.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.200
We look for the product of two numbers which gives us 181.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.760
This is how the product should look.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:39.740
What number do you think we can write in the boxes to get 181 as our product?

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:44.080
Remember, the digits in both the boxes have to be the same.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.540
Yes!

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:49.820
181 multiplied by 1 gives us 181.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.780
So we have found the digit in the boxes, it's 1.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:57.360
After we find this digit we go back to the third step

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.580
and follow the same procedure, multiply above.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:04.480
So we write a 1 and a 1 in these two boxes

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.940
and get the product of 181 and 1 as 181.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:15.060
Then we add below. We add 1 to 181 and get 182.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:19.040
Then we subtract the product from the number above it.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:23.920
So we subtract 181 from 181 and get a 0.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:28.780
The moment we get a 0 here and there are no more pairs left,

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.060
we are done!

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.120
But wait,

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.660
where's the square root of 8281.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.580
Well it's the number you got on top, it's 91.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:42.680
The square root of 8281 is 91.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:46.620
Trust me, it's not difficult. It's just a little lengthy.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.140
Let's review what we just did.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:54.840
We marked pairs from the unit's end which gave us two pairs 82 and 81.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.300
Then we choose a perfect square which is equal to

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:01.520
or lower than the leftmost pair 82.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:05.240
We found out that 81 is the closest square

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:09.640
We write its square root to the left then we multiply above.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:17.320
9 x 9 equals 81 and added below 9 plus 9 equals 18.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:21.900
And with 18, we leave space for one more digit.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:24.960
Then we reach the three simple steps.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:30.500
First, we subtract the product 82 minus 81 gives us 1.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:32.840
Second, we get the next pair down.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:36.660
And then we draw the same box above and below,

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:40.040
which will contain the same digit as the original box.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:44.440
And to find the digit in the boxes we use trial and error

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.500
and get 181 multiplied by 1 as 181.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:51.660
So the number in the box will be 1.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:55.500
After we find the number in the box we go back to the third step.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:57.820
We multiply above.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:03.740
181 multiplied by 1 gives us 181, then we add the same digit below

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:07.620
181 plus one equals 182.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.840
Then we subtract the product.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.980
181 minus 181 gives us 0.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:20.200
And since there is no pair left, we stop and get the square root as 91.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:24.560
Remember, inside the two lines, we always subtract.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:27.320
And outside, we always add.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.280
To get a better idea,

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:30.980
see the second part of this video,

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:34.140
in which we have solved for the square root of another number

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.360
using the same procedure.

